/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Example_LUTVolume Volume
 * @ingroup DspCore_Examples_LUT
 * @brief Exercise 3D table indexing, move semantics and rejected impossible shapes.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTVolume_Goal Goal
 * Populate a 2-by-3-by-4 volume, move its storage, reject a shape whose product
 * would overflow, and release an empty volume safely.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTVolume_Run Run
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_LUT_Volume_d
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTVolume_Output Output
 * @code{.text}
 * 2x3x4 volume: (1,2,3)=123; expected=123
 * Move transferred storage and cleared source: PASS
 * Overflow rejected; shape and sample preserved: PASS
 * Empty resize and repeated Release: PASS
 * Overall: PASS
 * @endcode
 *
 * The failed resize is intentionally non-destructive: the previously valid
 * table remains available to the caller.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTVolume_Code Implementation
 * \include LUT/Volume/Shared.cpp
 */
